## gllvmTMB licensing
##
## gllvmTMB is a standalone Template Model Builder (TMB) package for
## stacked-trait, long-format multivariate generalised linear latent
## variable models (GLLVMs). The gllvmTMB-specific code -- the
## multi-trait engine in src/gllvmTMB.cpp, the formula
## parser, the 4 x 5 covariance keyword grid, the per-trait response
## families (including ordinal_probit), the diagnostic and extractor
## machinery -- is licensed GPL-3 by Shinichi Nakagawa.
##
## The R-side spatial helpers in R/mesh.R, R/crs.R, and R/plot.R are
## independently authored gllvmTMB GPL-3 code. They use the public fmesher
## API and the published SPDE/GMRF construction; no sdmTMB source code is
## included or adapted.
##
## TMB engine (src/gllvmTMB.cpp)
##
## The C++ template under src/gllvmTMB.cpp is original gllvmTMB-
## native code by Shinichi Nakagawa, written against the TMB API
## (Kristensen et al. 2016, https://github.com/kaskr/adcomp). TMB is
## a runtime dependency (Imports + LinkingTo in DESCRIPTION) rather
## than included source.
##
## Upstream copyright holder of TMB:
##
##   * Kasper Kristensen (TMB author, https://github.com/kaskr/adcomp)
##
## TMB itself is GPL-2/GPL-3 licensed. See the upstream TMB
## DESCRIPTION at https://github.com/kaskr/adcomp for the full TMB
## author list.
##
## Sparse phylogenetic precision builder (R/phylo-tree-precision.R)
##
## The tree -> sparse A^{-1} construction in R/phylo-tree-precision.R
## (`.gllvm_phylo_tree_precision()` and its validators
## `.gllvm_validate_phylo_tree()` / `.gllvm_validate_phylo_species()` /
## `.gllvm_phylo_node_depths()` / `.gllvm_phylo_augmented_node_labels()`)
## is ported from the univariate sister package drmTMB
## (R/phylo-utils.R: `drm_phylo_augmented_precision()` and helpers).
## It uses only `ape` + `Matrix` and replaces the earlier
## MCMCglmm::inverseA() call on the `phylo_latent(tree = ...)` path, so
## MCMCglmm is no longer required to turn a tree into A^{-1}. Both
## gllvmTMB and drmTMB are GPL-3 by Shinichi Nakagawa (same-author
## reuse); the algorithm is the standard Hadfield & Nakagawa (2010)
## sparse phylogenetic inverse.
##
## Sparse pedigree precision builder (R/pedigree-precision.R)
##
## The pedigree -> sparse A^{-1} construction in R/pedigree-precision.R
## (`.gllvm_pedigree_precision()` and its helpers
## `.gllvm_standardize_pedigree()` / `.gllvm_normalize_pedigree_parent()` /
## `.gllvm_pedigree_topological_order()` /
## `.gllvm_pedigree_additive_relationship()`) reuses the pedigree
## standardisation, missing-parent normalisation, topological ordering,
## and dense tabular relatedness method ported from the univariate sister
## package drmTMB (R/phylo-utils.R: `drm_standardize_pedigree()`,
## `drm_normalize_pedigree_parent()`, `drm_pedigree_topological_order()`,
## `drm_pedigree_additive_relationship()`), which never depended on
## MCMCglmm. The sparse A^{-1} is then assembled on top via the standard
## Henderson (1976) / Quaas (1976) inverse rules. It uses only `Matrix`
## and replaces the earlier MCMCglmm::inverseA() call in
## `pedigree_to_Ainv_sparse()`, so MCMCglmm is no longer required to turn
## a pedigree into A^{-1}. Both gllvmTMB and drmTMB are GPL-3 by Shinichi
## Nakagawa (same-author reuse). The result is validated to reproduce
## `MCMCglmm::inverseA()` (Hadfield 2010) exactly, including inbreeding.
